  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sky wave propagation is used by short wave broadcast services having a frequency range from few&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MHz</mi></math>&nbsp;up to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math></p><p>Long-distance communication can be achieved by ionosphere reflection of radio waves back towards the earth as shown in Fig. This mode of propagation is called skywave propagation.</p><p><img alt=\"\" height=\"209\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/IL0003553_AnsExp3_1.png\" width=\"416\" /></p>",
